<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ralph Abercromby</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1734">1734</a>–<a href="/years/1801">1801</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Sir Ralph Abercromby</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sir Ralph Abercromby was a Scottish general of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolutionary-wars">French Revolutionary Wars</a>. In 1797 he led the British expedition that captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trinidad">Trinidad</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, beginning British rule there. He was mortally wounded in 1801 at the Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a>, where his army defeated the French forces left in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ralph-abercromby.jpg" alt="Ralph Abercromby" width="320" height="378" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: After John Hoppner · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sir_Ralph_Abercromby_by_John_Hoppner.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
